When a UNIX process crashes the OS (under usual conditions)
creates a 'core' file, containing memory image of the process
at the time of the crash in the (then) current working directory.

Assuming you have such a 'core' file, you can do

   ladebug /path/to/executable core

and use ladebug to figure out what happened.




