Brian Beuchaw wrote:
> 
> Hello all,
> 
> I've been searching the web/Usenet for a couple of hours and can't find a
> quick how-to guide on this - I've got an Alphaserver DS20 with an
> Intraserver SCSI/Ethernet card in it and the Ethernet part got fried (MAC
> address is wonky), so I found a DE500-BA that I stuck in the server.  SRM
> recognizes it, but nothing else does.  

Do a uerf -Rr 300 | more and watch carefully tu1.  If it doesn't show up, try
shutting down and powering off the box completely before rebooting.

Assuming that Tru64 actually see tu1, there is really no way that I know of to
"disable" tu0 so just move your address from tu0 to tu1.  In /etc/rc.config set
NUM_NETCONFIG="2" and NETDEV_1="tu1".  Set IFCONFIG_1 to the value of IFCONFIG_0 and
change IFCONFIG_0 to some address no one else is using.

Reboot.  Check your handiwork with ifconfig -a

>AIX, Linux, etc. seem to do this nicely, but Tru64 seems to be a bit of a pain. :-(


If you want to run Linux or AIX do so.  If you get paid to support Tru64 RTFM (man 
network_manual_setup).



Live long and prosper.


