Shawn wrote:

> Just curious if anyone has had similar problems.  In one of our data
> centers, some of our alpha systems lose network connectivity.  What we
> end up doing is just a simple "rcinet restart" and then the system
> continues working.

Losing network connectivity is sort-of a vague description of a
problem, can you answer a few questions?.  Are all connections
hung or is it just that new ones can't be created (maybe inetd)?
Can you reach some systems but not others (routing problem)?
Do you have a lot of host routes on your system with the destination
and gateway the same (icmp redirect problem)?
Do you have permanent ARP entries that are getting modified
(ARP problem)?

If you have the latest patch kit, inetd probably isn't at fault.
Random routing problems can't always be explained easily,
you'd have to look at the routing table and gated log (if you're
running it) to see what was added/deleted and why.  There
was a recent bug with Cisco access boxes sending bogus
icmp redirects causing us to add invalid routes - you can
contact the support people to get a patch for "stricter"
redirect processing code.  There is also a patch available
to make sure we don't update permanent ARP entries.

If you have any further info, post it here and I can try
and make sense of it Monday, but those are the only
"hot" ones I know about.

-Brian

