On Thu, 13 Sep 2001 jmfbahciv@aol.com wrote:

> In article <3B9FB85C.B0647513@mediaone.net>,
>    Bob Willard <bobwbsgs@mediaone.net> wrote:
> >
> >Dave also personally wrote a lot of the SMP code for VMS, from his
> >office in ZSO; 
> 
> How do you know this?
> 
> > ..after Dick had said that VMS was ASMP forever.
> 
> Dick declared that right after he had his meetings with JMF
> and TW who did do TOPS-10 SMP.

Cutler was known for doing end runs around management.  When Marketing
tried to justify the price differential between RSX-11D and RSX-11M by
saying that the smaller -11M wouldn't access the entire memory of the
bigger pdp-11's, Cutler issued his own press release, both internally and
externally, and said "They're lying to you -- 11M will do everything -11D
will do."

> >I contend that the SMPization of VMS is the work of a real programmer.
> 
> I doubt it was Cutler who did the work; the timing is all wrong.

Does that change if you consider that if he was convinced that it was the
*RIGHT* thing to do (for VMS) he'd go do it himself anyway?  _That_ would
be vintage Cutler.  But I'm less clear on the dates of all this, so merely
pose it as a devil's advocate.

-- 
I liked HP before computers, and at one time I liked Compaq,
but I liked DEC better than HP and Compaq put together.




