I assume this is a SCSI HW Raid, not PCI nor EISA.

if you reboot the new system, just connect your RAID box, check at the
console level that you see your devices :

>>> show dev
and boot

/dev/MAKEDEV won't be necessary, devices will be crated at boot.

If you warm connect to a SCSI bus, scan the busses ( #scu scan edt )
and create
the devices with /dev/MAKEDEV

if you have an LSM structure, if it is self contained in the box
within a disk group, and if it is not roodg, it is fairly easy.

if lsm is running yet on your system, just voldisk define the new
devices and import the disk group.
if lsm is not setup, set it up on a partition using volsetup, voldisk
define and import disk group.

then creates the advfs structure in /etc/fdmns, using a link to
/dev/DGNAME/vol instead of standard device.

god luck

