The project to develop a portable kernel around which a new Super-VMS
would be built. Cutler took the source-code lock, stock and barrel
with him to Microsoft after the project was canceled and used it as
the basis of the NT kernel. PRISM was the parallel hardware project
canceled at the same time. When Alpha rose from the ashes of PRISM and
DEC started ported NT to Alpha they advertised the Alpha as "born to
run NT" because of this. When Compaq killed NT I asked them how this
fitted in with the "born to run NT" claim. Less than two years later
we found out.

Cutler laughed in DEC's face when they started porting NT to Alpha by
saying something like "These idiots are now paying for something they
once had free". He also began the porting work himself just to further
annoy DEC and by the time the sources reached DEC they found he had
'helped' the port by using the code names for various parts of the
MICA/PRISM projects all over the Alpha source tree and, worse, that
the base code was updated versions of MICA. DEC Complained to Gates
but did not talk any legal action. Documented in "Showstopper" - the
story of Windows NT. The book is almost as much a biography of Cutler
as it s of NT.

>/BAH
