In article <2f6bec0a.0109110033.1524ae09@posting.google.com> banny52@yahoo.com (Ginny E. Kim) writes:
>I need to change open_max_hard, open_max_soft..
>But, "sysconfig -r proc open_max_soft=8196" gave me following message,
>"open_max_soft: attribute does not allow this operation".
>
>Can't the value of "open_max_soft" be changed by the command of
>"sysconfig"?
>And, After I add the value of "open_max_soft" on "/etc/sysconfigtab"
>and reboot the my system.. But, I can't get changed value of
>"open_max_soft"..
>How can it be changed?

open_max_soft can be set in /etc/sysconfigtab to take effect at boot
time, but cannot be changed at run time with sysconfig.

To check variables, use:

# sysconfig -Q proc open_max_soft
proc:
open_max_soft -         type=INT op=CQ min_val=0 max_val=4096
# 

This says that it is of type "int", the supported operations are
Configure and Query (NOTE: not Reconfigure), and the limits are 0->4096

