> cbriel@olgc.on.ca (Chris) writes:
> 
>> We are upgrading our OS from digital unix 4.0d to 5.1 and are
>> currently running Sybase ASE 11.9.2.  OS 5.1 changes the physical
>> device names.  Since we are using raw partitions for devices in our
>> Sybase servers, what is the easiest way to migrate with little or no
>> impact.
> 
> Don't migrate. Or migrate to V4.0F instead.
> 
> Is there a reason that you *want* to migrate to 5.1?
> 
> Joel

If you had sybase on LSM you wouldn't have this trouble but since you don't
just make symbolic links in /dev for what ever your current sysdevices has
recorded.  Start the server allow updates to system tables update sysdevices
with the new device names update the server run script to point to the new
device name of the master devices, shutdown the server, remove the links
from /dev and everything should be fine.


