accustomed to still being able to run OS/360 programs natively on 21st
century IBM hardware; for that matter, it might even turn off PC types used
to being able to run DOS programs on modern hardware.

Most people weren't that upset when migrating from VAX to Alpha because
Alpha offered improved performance to compensate for the effort.  But moving
from EV7 to McKinley or Madison may well be an actual performance
