Tru64 autofs is inspired by Solaris autofs but is an independent
implementation.  I don't think either one does loopback NFS mounts.

Even if autofs did a loopback NFS mount, you haven't stated a problem.
Loopback NFS mounts used to cause deadlock, and that would be a problem.
Poor performance would be a problem (autofs was supposed to improve
performance).  All you have identified is a pathname different than
you expected.



