Dmitry Vjushin <vjushin@ory.ph.biu.ac.il> wrote:
: Hi, Gurus !

: I have a NIS server running on AU500 with 4.0D and several NIS clients on 
: 4.0A, 4.0D, 4.0F. I've created a new NIS  user today. On NIS server new 
: account works perfect, but when I tried to login to any of NIS clients 
: it shows me the error message "Account is disabled -- see Account Administrator".
: When I use SSH to login remotely, it shows "Authentication successful."
: and again the same error message after that.
: Could you please help me to resolve this problem ?

: Thanks in advance,
: Dmitry

: P.S. Linux NIS client works well as before.

This is a problem with the Enhanced security user profiles, the prpasswd
database. You can look and edit the prpasswd entry in the NIS server
with the command edauth. Clearly the username and password are working
correctly, but something else is wrong. Most common reason is too
many login attempts with a wrong password, the u_numunsuclog field
in the prpasswd database. The mystery here is, why the account works
in the NIS server. Does the NIS server have different Enhanced security
defaults?


