Hi,

I recently discovered a neat utility called dxkeycaps on my AlphaServer DS20
which is running Tru64 V5.0A.  dxkeycaps allows you to interactively edit the
keyboard mapping.  I used it to redefine the top row on the numeric keypad to
act like the PF1 - PF4 keys on a VT100 keyboard.  Now I can telnet from the
alpha to a VMS system and the keypad works correctly in the editor (EDT). 
dxkeycaps created a file (.dxkeycaps, in my home directory) which contained the
following lines used to redefine the keypad keys:
	keycode 0x76 = KP_F1 KP_F1
	keycode 0x77 = KP_F2 KP_F2
	keycode 0x7E = KP_F3 KP_F3
	keycode 0x84 = KP_F4 KP_F4

Does anyone know if I can do the same thing in Solaris?  I would like to be able
to telnet from my sun to a VMS system and edit using the keypad.  I found a
program called loadkeys which looks like it might work, but I don't know how to
redefine the keys to be PF1 - PF4.  I imagine suns don't know about PF1, PF2,
PF3, PF4 (?)

Thanks for any help!
Ginny


