believe here at the INQUIRER that the Round Rock firm is in a very
powerful position to swat Carly's outfit when IT recovery comes. HP
will be involved in a good old bit of navel gazing which is bound to
take its eye off the ball for months and months to come.

OpenVMS and the other corporate elements of Compaq's business would
now seem to come under HP's wing.

How corporate and federal customers will react to that remains to be
seen - Compaq did give a solemn commitment that it would carry on
supporting and developing these OSes.

