Follow up to my own question.  Networking is setup fine now.  Problem
was the Kingston 21140-based card.  Although SRM recognized it OK, and
Tru64 appeared to have configured it, I couldn't ping anything. 
Replacing it with an older Tulip NIC on a Qlogic combo card fixed the
problem, and connecting to the Internet took two steps.

1)  editing three files:  /etc/rc.config, /etc/hosts, and /etc/routes
(manual edit because netconfig GUI doesn't allow 192.168.0.x
addressing)

2)  Using the GUI-based DNS configuration to add the IP addresses for
the two DNS from my ISP.  I was a bit confused by the "domain name"
entry that is required, as I didn't have to enter this on Win or Linux
clients in the Ethernet.  I ended up just typing "localhost", as I
really didn't want it to search the local domain at all.  Not really
sure what I was doing, but seems to work OK.

Thanks to those who sent advice.

